WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
If you used to edit transforms from the
Traffic tab, open Prepare on your

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.280
snapshot.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.400
Let's take the same rule through both
editors.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.840
This one swaps the order request's routing
mode for a sandbox value before replay.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.480
In the old drawer, Subset told you which
requests the rule applied to.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:23.040
Source pointed at the request body, and
Transform held the steps.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.672
You read the chain string at the top and
opened the individual controls to check

00:00:27.672 --> 00:00:29.120
what each step was doing.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.615
In Prepare, choose Tests for requests
Speedscale sends to your app, or Mocks for

00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:35.920
dependency traffic.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:39.680
Open a rule under In this snapshot and
read down the middle.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:44.160
Runs on is the old subset. Pull from is
the old source.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.840
Then come the numbered steps and where the
result gets written back.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.640
Click a step to edit it in place. Use a
plus between steps to insert one

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.160
or drag a step to change the order. Here,
JSON Path has to come first.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.080
It selects the routing mode so Constant
can replace that one value.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.700
Pick a recorded request on the right.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:10.628
The preview shows the whole body coming
in, the original mode after JSON Path, and

00:01:10.628 --> 00:01:12.100
sandbox after Constant.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.807
At the bottom, Replay uses shows the full
body again, with sandbox in the right

00:01:17.807 --> 00:01:18.180
field.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.620
Click another request to check the same
rule against a different sample.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:28.620
Suggestions that used to live in Tuning or
Recommendations are now under To review.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:32.620
You can see what a suggestion does to a
sample before you accept it.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:34.620
Accept adds it to your draft.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.620
Save and reanalyze applies the staged
changes together.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.620
To double-check a saved change, go back to
Traffic and open the request.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.620
Compare shows the recording beside the
result of the saved transforms.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.620
If you're still editing, use the preview
in Prepare to see your draft.
